You are given a task to integrate a component from the **kinetik** motion library into this codebase.

# Password Peek (`input-password-peek`)

Password field with character: an eye whose lid opens to reveal — letters scramble from dots into real characters left-to-right — and closes to hide; the pupil follows the caret as you type.

## What it should do
Build a password-peek input: a real input with transparent text and a visible caret, overlaid by a mono span showing either dots or the value; toggling reveal scrambles characters (random glyphs settling left→right over 350 ms). The toggle is an SVG eye whose lid (pupil group) scales on Y open/closed with a spring and whose pupil moves with the text length.

## Project requirements
- React 19 + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui-style CSS variables (`background`, `foreground`, `muted`, `muted-foreground`, `border`, `card`, `primary`, `ring`). If the project lacks shadcn, set it up first (`npx shadcn@latest init`).
- Animation engine: **motion**.
- Install dependencies: `npm i motion`
- Put the component at `components/kinetik/input-password-peek.tsx`.
- `cn` lives at `lib/kinetik/utils.ts` (source below).
- Shared hooks go at `lib/kinetik/core.ts` (source below).

## Non-negotiables
- **Accessibility:** Real password input underneath (autofill and managers work); toggle is aria-pressed with a label; character count announced. Reduced motion: instant swap.
- **Performance:** Scramble runs ~350 ms only on toggle.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (replace movement with opacity or an instant change).
- Animate only transform / opacity / filter / clip-path. No hard-coded theme colors — use CSS variables so it works in light and dark.

